<title>INDIA: India RBI sets 5.0 percent cut-off at repo auction.</title>
<headline>India RBI sets 5.0 percent cut-off at repo auction.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off interest rate of 5.0 percent at Thursday's repo auction.</p>
<p>The cut-off at the earlier auction on Monday was 5.25 percent. The next repo auction is on Saturday, January 18.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it received 42 bids for 28.60 billion rupees of which it accepted 33 bids for 22.50 billion rupees.</p>
<p>The weighted average price was 4.3423 percent, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
